    },
    {
      "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@21876",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BOTTOM.\nI will discharge it in either your straw-colour beard, your orange-tawny beard, your purple-in-grain beard, or your French-crown-colour beard, your perfect yellow.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@21876/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@21876/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 171,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 4247940,
        "end": 4248143,
        "line": 157304,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap24/p@21876",
        "anchor": "sceneI_24.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "BOTTOM.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@22083",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "QUINCE.\nSome of your French crowns have no hair at all, and then you will play bare-faced. But, masters, here are your parts, and I am to entreat you, request you, and desire you, to con them by tomorrow night; and meet me in the palace wood, a mile without the town, by moonlight; there will we rehearse, for if we meet in the city, we shall be dogg’d with company, and our devices known. In the meantime I will draw a bill of properties, such as our play wants. I pray you fail me not.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@22083/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@22083/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 487,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 4248147,
        "end": 4248670,
        "line": 157311,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap24/p@22083",
        "anchor": "sceneI_24.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "QUINCE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@22610",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BOTTOM.\nWe will meet, and there we may rehearse most obscenely and courageously. Take pains, be perfect; adieu.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream/sceneI_24.2/p@22610/line-1",
